senses.gloss:
√tyaj (tyájati, -te; tatyā́ja, tatyajé;
átyākṣīt; tyakṣyáti, -te; tyaktá; tyáktum;
tyaktvā́; -tyájya; tyajyáte; tyājáyati).
--1. withdraw from; leave in the
lurch; abandon (dove, goat, tree);
 —2. renounce
(passions, use of a language);
relinquish (exertion); lay aside (a certain
form, an earthly body); set aside, i. e. risk
(life). [cf. σέβομαι, ‘shrink back from in
awe, revere.’]
+ pari, leave to one's fate (a jackal);
abandon; leave (one's party); relinquish
or give up (play, food, affairs); parityakta,
(abandoned by, i. e.) separated
from, 66^3.
